{"id": "rp3-00464", "q": "What is 75 times 93?", "a": "To calculate $75 \\times 93$, we can break the problem down using the distributive property or standard multiplication.\n\n**Method 1: Breaking it down**\nWe can split 93 into 90 and 3:\n$$75 \\times 93 = 75 \\times (90 + 3)$$\n$$= (75 \\times 90) + (75 \\times 3)$$\n\n1.  Calculate $75 \\times 90$:\n    $$75 \\times 9 = 675$$\n    So, $75 \\times 90 = 6750$\n\n2.  Calculate $75 \\times 3$:\n    $$75 \\times 3 = 225$$\n\n3.  Add the results together:\n    $$6750 + 225 = 6975$$\n\n**Method 2: Standard Multiplication**\n```text\n    75\n  x 93\n  ----\n   225   (75 * 3)\n 6750    (75 * 90)\n  ----\n 6975\n```\n\n**Answer:**\n75 times 93 is **6,975**."}
{"id": "rp3-00465", "q": "Add 43 and 56.", "a": "To add 43 and 56, you can break it down by place value:\n\n1.  **Add the ones place:** $3 + 6 = 9$\n2.  **Add the tens place:** $40 + 50 = 90$\n3.  **Combine the results:** $90 + 9 = 99$\n\nAlternatively, using column addition:\n$$\n\\begin{array}{c@{\\,}c@{\\,}c}\n & \\mathbf{1} & \\\\\n4 & 3 & + \\\\\n5 & 6 & \\overline{=} \\\\\n\\hline\n9 & 9 &\n\\end{array}\n$$\n\nThe sum of 43 and 56 is **99**."}
{"id": "rp3-00466", "q": "Add 80 and 3.", "a": "To add 80 and 3, you simply combine the two numbers:\n\n$$80 + 3 = 83$$\n\nThe result is **83**."}
